    "body": "The following changes are made to enable `inference_core_ops ` extension on `ROCm`:\r\n\r\n- Compile the ROCm HIP kernels as `C++20` when PyTorch is 2.12 or newer. \r\n\r\n- Under` hipBLAS v2`, use `hipDataType` for the GEMM datatype. hipify was turning `cublasDataType_t ` into `hipblasDatatype_t`, which this hipBLAS no longer defines.\r\n\r\n- On AMD, pass a 64-bit mask to `__shfl_sync `in the FP6 dequant kernel. 0xffffffff is a 32-bit unsigned int, and this HIP build rejects it.\r\n\r\n- Pass `QUANT_GEMM_Kernel ` to `cudaFuncSetAttribute` through a concrete function pointer. After hipify, `hipFuncSetAttribute` only accepts `const void*`, and the `__global__` template did not convert. On CUDA, `cudaFuncSetAttribute` still sets `cudaFuncAttributeMaxDynamicSharedMemorySize` on the same kernel.\r\n\r\n- PyTorch's hipify keeps the `.cpp` extension and appends _hip to the stem, so `bias_activation.cpp` becomes `bias_activation_hip.cpp`. The CUDA source `bias_activation_cuda.cu` becomes `bias_activation_hip.hip`, which has the same stem. Both compile to `bias_activation_hip.o`, and that duplicate object caused the link error. Renaming the host file to `bias_activation_host.cpp` gives `bias_activation_host_hip.cpp` and avoids the clash. Thee same changes are made to `gated_activation_kernels.cpp` file too.\r\n  - deepspeed/inference/v2/kernels/core_ops/bias_activations/bias_activation.cpp → bias_activation_host.cpp\r\n   - deepspeed/inference/v2/kernels/core_ops/gated_activations/gated_activation_kernels.cpp → gated_activation_kernels_host.cpp\r\n\r\n## Test\r\nJIT Build\r\n```\r\nimport deepspeed.ops.op_builder as op_builder\r\nop_builder.InferenceCoreBuilder().load()           # inference_core_ops\r\n```\r\n\r\nnon-JIT Build\r\n```\r\ncd DeepSpeed\r\nDS_BUILD_OPS=0 DS_BUILD_INFERENCE_CORE_OPS=1 python3 setup.py build_ext --inplace\r\n```",
